  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "Soak the cedar plank in water for 30 minutes before use. ",
    "Season the sea bass fillets with salt, black pepper, and Italian seasoning. ",
    "Place the cedar plank on a baking sheet and arrange the sea bass fillets on the plank. ",
    "Drizzle the top of the sea bass with olive oil and lemon juice. ",
    "Bake in the preheated oven for 12 minutes. ",
    "While the sea bass is baking, cook the penne pasta according to package instructions. ",
    "Melt the unsalted butter in a saucepan over medium heat. ",
    "Add the garlic, lemon zest, and red pepper flakes to the saucepan and cook for 1 minute, until fragrant. ",
    "Add the cooked penne pasta to the saucepan and toss with the melted butter and garlic mixture. ",
    "Season the pasta with salt, black pepper, and Italian seasoning to taste. ",
    "Chop the fresh parsley and basil and sprinkle over the pasta. ",
    "Place the cooked sea bass fillets on top of the pasta. ",
    "Serve immediately, garnished with additional parsley and basil if desired. ",
    "Cover the baking sheet with aluminum foil and bake for an additional 2 minutes, until the fish is cooked through.",
    "Let the sea bass rest for 2 minutes before placing on top of the pasta."
  ],
